HTMLPCBViewer bundles and derives from third-party MIT-licensed code.
Their copyright and permission notices are reproduced below, as MIT requires.

Where the code comes from:

  web/render.js, web/render-worker.js
      Derived from InteractiveHtmlBom web/render.js. Split into a main-thread
      coordinator and an OffscreenCanvas worker; drawing primitives, path
      building and hit-testing are largely upstream.

  web/app.js
      Derived in part from InteractiveHtmlBom web/ibom.js and web/table-util.js.

  web/util.js
      Derived in part from InteractiveHtmlBom web/util.js.

  web/viewer.css
      Derived in part from InteractiveHtmlBom web/ibom.css.

  web/split.js
      Split.js v1.3.5, vendored unmodified as shipped by InteractiveHtmlBom.

  allegro-skills/jsonDecode.il
      From juulsA/exportJson, unmodified.

  allegro-skills/exportJson.il
      From juulsA/exportJson, with local modifications.

The JSON data format is InteractiveHtmlBom's, documented in its DATAFORMAT.md.

